# Naryad No1007 (issue #2078, volna В106 — W4 follow-up): the S3.4 pinned
# examples must survive byte-identical on EVERY checkout lane. The GitHub
# Windows runners configure core.autocrlf=true, which converts LF to CRLF
# on checkout and breaks the sha256 pin identity (the first cross run
# 45549890075: workload PIN MISMATCH — the tripwire held, no numbers
# recorded). Scoped to exactly the two pinned files: NOT a repo-wide
# text=auto normalization — file trees are never rewritten silently.
# The linux lanes are unaffected (the index blobs are already LF).
examples/dag_demo.mlog text eol=lf
examples/dag_demo.expected text eol=lf
